TEMPLATE=(ROOT/'how-we-work/how-ae-tax-advisors-approaches-engagements/index.html').read_text()
STYLE=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',TEMPLATE,re.S).group(1)
NAV=re.search(r'<nav class="nav">.*?</nav>',TEMPLATE,re.S).group(0).replace('<a href="/guides/">','<a href="/case-studies/">Case Studies</a><a href="/guides/">')
FOOTER=re.search(r'<footer class="footer">.*?</footer>',TEMPLATE,re.S).group(0)
DISC='This resource is published by AE Tax Advisors. Case-study figures are publisher-reported and have not been independently audited here. They are not client reviews, typical results or a forecast for your return.'
GENERATED=[]

GROUPS=[
('short-term-rental','Short-Term Rental Case Studies', ['w2-couple-str-offset','physician-w2-str-reps','airbnb-arbitrage-operator-business-expense-optimization'],
'Start with how the owner earns income and how the property is used. An employee who owns a rental, a physician with several properties and an operator leasing units have different tax profiles. The arbitrage business in this collection does not own the buildings, so it should not be evaluated as though it can depreciate purchased real estate.',
'Do the booking records support the customer-use pattern? Who performed the work? Were the furnishings purchased by the operator? Does the proposed deduction survive the owner-level loss limitations?',
'Booking history, participation records, purchase or lease agreements, furnishing invoices, depreciation schedules and prior suspended losses.',
'A reported wage offset is not proof that every Airbnb owner can claim the same result. Ask the advisor to connect the projected deduction to your own participation facts and complete return. The excess business loss rules can matter even after nonpassive treatment is established.'),
('cost-segregation','Cost Segregation Case Studies',['self-storage-facility-cost-seg-automation','mobile-home-park-cost-seg-infrastructure','hotel-boutique-investor-cost-seg-ffe-energy-credits'],
'Cost segregation cases should be compared by the depreciable assets, ownership and service dates. A self-storage portfolio, manufactured housing community and boutique hotel contain very different improvements. Read the asset description before comparing the headline savings.',
'Is the reported amount a deduction or tax saving? Is it first-year acceleration or an annual figure? What basis was studied? When can the owner use the resulting loss?',
'Closing statements, land allocation, improvement invoices, existing depreciation schedules, engineering report, service dates and owner-return projections.',
'A building study addresses classification and timing. It does not establish that the entire deduction is usable immediately. An evaluation should separate the study deliverable, tax implementation work and any future recapture or timing effects.'),
('s-corporation','S Corporation Case Studies',['sole-prop-to-s-corp-contractor','s-corp-officer-comp-correction','s-corp-payroll-setup-sole-prop','s-corp-late-election-relief'],
'An S corporation decision includes payroll, reasonable compensation, filing obligations and the owner’s actual work. A profitable contractor considering an election needs a different review from an existing shareholder correcting payroll or seeking late-election relief.',
'Which legal entity exists? What is the election’s effective date? How was compensation evaluated? What payroll and preparation costs were included in the savings comparison?',
'Entity documents, election acceptance, owner job description, compensation support, payroll filings, business returns and distributions ledger.',
'Do not copy a compensation percentage from a published case. The IRS analysis depends on services, responsibilities and other facts. A case is a useful prompt for questions, not a salary schedule for another business.'),
('c-corporation','C Corporation Case Studies',['s-corp-to-c-corp-medical','medical-practice-c-corp-retirement-stacking','private-medical-practice-c-corp-defined-benefit'],
'C corporation planning should consider where profits are earned, retained and eventually distributed. The medical-practice cases illustrate why retirement design, employee costs and the owner’s future cash needs belong in the same discussion as the corporation’s income tax.',
'What business purpose supports the structure? Are related-party payments supported by actual services? What happens when the owner withdraws profits? Which benefits and plan contributions are really available?',
'Ownership chart, service agreements, payroll, employee census, retirement-plan proposals, retained-earnings forecast and distribution assumptions.',
'A corporate tax rate alone is not a complete result. Ask for a multi-year comparison including shareholder tax, administration and the use of retained cash. A published case does not establish that forming a C corporation is appropriate for every high-income owner.'),
('medical-dental','Medical and Dental Practice Case Studies',['dental-practice-cost-seg-entity-restructuring','private-medical-practice-c-corp-defined-benefit','physician-reps-qualification-cost-seg-combo','veterinary-practice-cost-seg-section-179'],
'Practice owners can have operating income, owned premises, equipment, employees and outside investments. These cases help separate the tax treatment of the practice from the treatment of real estate owned alongside it. The physician rental example also requires its own participation facts.',
'Who owns the practice building? Which entity employs staff? What funding commitment accompanies the retirement proposal? Which rental activities were analyzed separately?',
'Practice financial statements, entity returns, building basis, equipment invoices, employee census, compensation records and property activity documentation.',
'Two owners with the same profession can have different results because their age, staff, ownership and cash needs differ. Ask for a plan that identifies those differences explicitly rather than treating an industry label as eligibility.'),
('retirement-planning','Retirement Planning Case Studies',['law-firm-partner-s-corp-cash-balance-plan','private-medical-practice-c-corp-defined-benefit','medical-practice-c-corp-retirement-stacking'],
'A retirement contribution reduces current spendable cash while potentially changing the tax calculation. The law-practice and medical cases are useful starting points for discussing age, compensation, employees and long-term funding expectations with a plan specialist.',
'Is the contribution a projection or a final actuarial recommendation? What employee contributions are required? Who administers the plan? What recurring costs and funding obligations apply?',
'Employee census, ages, compensation, existing plan documents, prior contributions, actuarial proposal, funding calendar and expected business cash flow.',
'A contribution is not itself a tax saving. Separate the dollars funded, the tax effect, the administrative cost and future withdrawal treatment. A large contribution in one case is not a universal annual limit for all owners.'),
('construction-trades','Construction and Contractor Case Studies',['construction-company-equipment-depreciation-entity-layering','sole-prop-to-s-corp-contractor','landscaping-contractor-section-179-stacking'],
'Contractors often combine equipment purchases, seasonal income, vehicles and owner labor. These cases are helpful for comparing a change in entity treatment with depreciation and expense decisions. They should not be reduced to a single instruction to buy equipment at year-end.',
'When was the equipment ready and available for business use? What is the business-use percentage? How much profit remains after payroll? Were financing and operating cash needs modeled?',
'Equipment invoices, service records, financing agreements, mileage records, job-cost reports, compensation support and current-year profit forecasts.',
'Buying an asset spends money even when it produces a deduction. Compare the after-tax cost of equipment needed by the business with the tax effect. Delivery, a deposit and placed-in-service status are different facts.'),
('ecommerce','E-Commerce Case Studies',['ecommerce-amazon-fba-s-corp','ecommerce-dropship-multistate','ecommerce-sole-prop-to-s-corp-entity-restructuring'],
'An online business’s tax picture includes inventory, marketplace activity, owner compensation and operations across jurisdictions. The FBA, dropshipping and direct-to-consumer cases offer different fact patterns rather than one model for every internet seller.',
'Where is inventory held? Which marketplace reports reconcile to the books? What state activity requires separate review? Does the entity comparison include payroll and filing costs?',
'Marketplace statements, sales reports, inventory schedules, state registrations, entity documents, payroll and bank reconciliation.',
'A federal planning result does not resolve every state filing obligation. Ask the advisor to distinguish income tax, sales tax and marketplace responsibilities. A case about another selling platform is not evidence of your business’s nexus facts.'),
('professional-services','Professional Services Case Studies',['law-firm-partner-s-corp-cash-balance-plan','tech-consulting-firm-ic-classification-accountable-plan','marketing-agency-home-office-augusta-rule-s-corp','insurance-agency-commission-entity-optimization'],
'A service firm’s economics depend heavily on who does the work. These cases cover partner income, contractors, employees, owner expenses and reimbursement. Evaluate the role of the owner and staff before comparing entity or retirement outcomes.',
'What services produce revenue? Which worker relationships were reviewed? How were personal and business expenses separated? Are reimbursements supported by an actual process?',
'Service contracts, worker agreements, payroll, owner duties, expense reports, reimbursement policy, home-office support and financial statements.',
'A label such as contractor, management fee or reimbursement does not settle the tax treatment. The underlying work, records and payment arrangement matter. Ask for a written explanation of the facts that support the proposed position.'),
('multi-entity','Multi-Entity Business Case Studies',['four-llc-consolidation-management-company','multi-entity-holding-company','multi-entity-real-estate-operating','husband-wife-three-businesses-joint-optimization'],
'Owners with multiple businesses need a consolidated picture before changing one entity. These cases show why operating profit, property ownership, payroll and household planning must be reconciled. More entities can also mean more returns, accounting work and agreements.',
'Which entity performs each function? Are intercompany balances reconciled? What economic reason supports a payment? How do changes affect both spouses and the owner-level return?',
'Ownership chart, all entity returns, intercompany agreements, bank accounts, payroll reports, property schedules and related-party balances.',
'Entity layering is not a result by itself. Compare the completed tax and cash picture before and after the proposed structure. Ask who will maintain the books and agreements after implementation and include that work in the cost comparison.'),
('rental-commercial-property','Rental and Commercial Property Case Studies',['ltr-section-1250-recapture-planning','triple-net-lease-passive-income-grouping-elections','self-storage-facility-cost-seg-automation','mobile-home-park-cost-seg-infrastructure'],
'Rental portfolios need planning over the holding period, including acquisition, operations and sale. The long-term rental, triple-net and specialized-property cases offer questions about depreciation, activity treatment and future disposition rather than just the first deduction.',
'What is the expected holding period? Which losses are suspended? What changes at sale? Are separate properties and entities being grouped or analyzed individually?',
'Lease agreements, acquisition records, depreciation schedules, participation workpapers, prior loss records, grouping disclosures and sale forecasts.',
'A larger first-year deduction can shift tax timing and affect later years. A decision should compare usable deductions now with future taxable income and sale consequences. Do not interpret an annual headline as a lifetime after-tax return.'),
('software-technology','Software and Technology Business Case Studies',['saas-founder-rd-credit-s-corp-optimization','tech-startup-rd-credit-qsbs','tech-founder-equity-comp-83b','manufacturing-company-rd-credit-macrs'],
'Technology cases can involve credits, equity compensation, development costs and owner payroll. Those are different tax systems, with different documentation and timing requirements. The reported result from an equity event should not be treated as interchangeable with a recurring operating deduction.',
'What expense or transaction created the tax effect? Which year’s law applies? What evidence supports the credit or election? Is the figure recurring, transactional or projected?',
'Development records, payroll allocations, expense ledgers, equity grant documents, election records, ownership history and transaction forecasts.',
'A founder should separate operating planning from equity and exit planning. Ask which recommendation needs a specialist review and which deadlines arise from a grant or transaction. A large headline is only useful once its measurement period and assumptions are clear.'),
]

def esc(s):return html.escape(str(s),quote=True)
def jl(d):return '<script type="application/ld+json">'+json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False)+'</script>'
def cards(items):return '<div class="rg">'+''.join(f'<a class="rc" href="{esc(url)}"><strong>{esc(title)}</strong><span>{esc(desc)}</span></a>' for url,title,desc in items)+'</div>'
def casecards(slugs):
    items=[]
    for slug in slugs:
        c=next(c for c in CASES if c['slug']==slug)
        items.append((c['url'],c['industry']+' case study',f'Publisher reports {c["headlineOutcome"]} in annual tax savings. Context: {c["keyMetric"]}. Read the source and assumptions.'))
    return cards(items)
def write(path,title,desc,body,faqs=None):
    faqs=faqs or [('Are these independently verified reviews?',DISC),('Can I expect the same savings?','No. The cases are selected examples. Your result depends on your facts, applicable law, implementation and the complete return.')]
    trail=[('Home','/'),('Case Studies','/case-studies/'),(title,path)]
    schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article','headline':title,'description':desc,'url':BASE+path,'mainEntityOfPage':BASE+path,'datePublished':DATE,'dateModified':DATE,'author':{'@type':'Organization','name':'AE Tax Advisors','url':AE},'publisher':{'@type':'Organization','name':'AE Tax Advisors','url':AE},'citation':[SOURCE]}
    faq={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage','mainEntity':[{'@type':'Question','name':q,'acceptedAnswer':{'@type':'Answer','text':a}} for q,a in faqs]}
    breadcrumb={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'BreadcrumbList','itemListElement':[{'@type':'ListItem','position':i+1,'name':n,'item':BASE+u} for i,(n,u) in enumerate(trail)]}
    text=f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{esc(title)} | AE Tax Advisors</title><meta name="description" content="{esc(desc)}"><link rel="canonical" href="{BASE+path}"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><meta property="og:title" content="{esc(title)}"><meta property="og:description" content="{esc(desc)}"><meta property="og:url" content="{BASE+path}"><meta property="og:type" content="article"><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">{jl(schema)}{jl(faq)}{jl(breadcrumb)}<style>{STYLE}\n.nav{{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:8px}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:1rem}}th,td{{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;vertical-align:top}}.table-wrap{{overflow-x:auto}}.content p,.content li{{font-size:1rem}}.case-disclosure{{font-size:1rem;padding:18px;background:#f5f6fa;margin:20px 0}}a:focus-visible{{outline:3px solid #e94560;outline-offset:3px}}</style></head><body>{NAV}<section class="hero"><h1>{esc(title)}</h1><p class="meta">By AE Tax Advisors | Updated September 30, 2026</p></section><div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/case-studies/">Case Studies</a></div><article class="content"><p class="case-disclosure">{DISC}</p>{body}<div class="faq"><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>'+''.join(f'<div class="faq-item"><h3>{esc(q)}</h3><p>{esc(a)}</p></div>' for q,a in faqs)+f'</div><h2>Sources and next steps</h2><p><a href="{SOURCE}">Read the AE Tax Advisors outcomes methodology</a>, the <a href="{AE}/case-studies/">original case studies</a> and the <a href="{AE}/pricing/">current pricing and scope</a>. The original return files and realization of reported savings have not been independently audited for this resource.</p><p><a href="/case-studies/">Browse all case-study guides</a> or <a href="/how-we-work/how-ae-tax-advisors-approaches-engagements/">read how an engagement is approached</a>.</p><div class="cta-box"><h2>Discuss your business or property</h2><p>Bring your returns, financial statements and questions. Ask which published example is relevant to your facts and what changes the analysis.</p><a class="btn" href="{AE}/discovery/">Book a Discovery Call</a></div></article>{FOOTER}</body></html>'
    target=ROOT/path.strip('/')/'index.html';target.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);target.write_text(text)
    GENERATED.append((path,title,desc))

def main():
    for slug,title,slugs,lead,questions,records,lesson in GROUPS:
        body=f'<p>{lead}</p><h2>Published AE Tax Advisors examples</h2>{casecards(slugs)}<h2>How to compare the cases</h2><p>{lesson}</p><p>Start with the baseline return and identify exactly what changed. Determine whether a reported amount refers to a deduction, a current tax difference or a projection over several years. Costs such as payroll, return preparation, a study fee and plan administration should be included in your own comparison.</p><h2>Questions for the discovery call</h2><p>{questions}</p><p>Ask for the assumptions in writing and for a separate list of facts still needed. A useful answer identifies both the potential opportunity and the work required to implement it. If an outside specialist must confirm a number, make that dependency visible in the plan.</p><h2>Records to prepare</h2><p>{records}</p><p>Use the most recent filed returns together with current financial information. Reconcile incomplete books before relying on a projection. Keep supporting records organized by entity and year so earlier deductions and carryforwards are not counted twice.</p><h2>What these cases tell you about engagement scope</h2><p>The collection gives you concrete topics to discuss with AE Tax Advisors. It does not establish what every advisory engagement includes. Confirm the analysis, implementation, tax-return work and continuing services in your own signed scope. The standard advertised advisory fee is $7,800 with no required recurring annual planning fee; separately scoped work can carry additional charges.</p>'
        write('/case-studies/'+slug+'/', 'AE Tax Advisors '+title,'Explore source-linked '+title.lower()+', reported outcomes, records and questions to ask before engaging AE Tax Advisors.',body)
    selected=[('w2-couple-str-offset','W-2 Couple and Short-Term Rental Loss','The source’s $195,000 rental paper-loss description should be read alongside the reported $68,000 annual tax savings. Those are different measures. The evaluation question is how the loss was usable on the owners’ complete return, not whether another couple can recreate the headline by purchasing a property.','Identify property use, participation, basis and the order of loss limitations before estimating a wage offset.'),('dental-practice-cost-seg-entity-restructuring','Dental Practice Building and Entity Planning','The source identifies $1.1 million of building basis and an owner age of 54. Building ownership and owner age are useful context because the cost of the property and retirement-planning profile can change the evaluation. They do not independently prove the reported tax result.','Separate property depreciation from operating-practice planning and identify which entity owns each asset.'),('private-medical-practice-c-corp-defined-benefit','Medical Practice and Defined Benefit Planning','The source describes four physician partners, average income of $680,000 each and 22 staff. This is an employer-plan and multi-owner context, not a one-person pension example. Employee costs and funding recommendations are central comparison questions.','Request an employee census analysis and final plan-administrator or actuarial recommendations before relying on a funding amount.'),('sole-prop-to-s-corp-contractor','Contractor Moving from Sole Proprietor to S Corporation','The source describes a reported change in self-employment tax together with a retirement-plan addition. The overall $41,000 headline should therefore not be treated as a standalone estimate of election savings for every contractor.','Compare compensation, payroll, entity-return costs and retirement funding within one owner-return model.'),('s-corp-officer-comp-correction','S Corporation Officer Compensation Correction','The source describes a compensation ratio changing from 3.4% to 7.3% of revenue. These ratios are facts reported about the case, not IRS-approved salary safe harbors. Copying either percentage into another owner’s payroll would skip the reasonable-compensation analysis.','Evaluate actual duties, time, experience and comparable compensation rather than setting wages from a case-study ratio.'),('self-storage-facility-cost-seg-automation','Self-Storage Facilities and Automation Equipment','The source describes 1,450 units, $4.8 million of combined building basis and $420,000 in automation equipment. Those facts distinguish several asset categories and operating locations. A headline cannot replace an asset-by-asset basis and tax-use review.','Separate building components, separately acquired equipment, service dates and the owner’s ability to use depreciation.'),('law-firm-partner-s-corp-cash-balance-plan','Law Firm Partner and Cash Balance Planning','The source identifies a partner age of 52, net income of $980,000 and three associates. The case can prompt questions about compensation, employees and retirement funding, but it does not establish another partner’s permitted contribution.','Model employee requirements, funding sustainability and administrative costs together with the tax deduction.'),('tech-consulting-firm-ic-classification-accountable-plan','Technology Consulting, Workers and Reimbursements','The source describes twelve contractors, four W-2 employees and owner income of $620,000. This is a useful reminder that worker treatment, payroll and owner reimbursement are distinct issues even when included in one engagement.','Review worker facts and expense substantiation separately before combining the results in a tax projection.')]
    for slug,label,analysis,lesson in selected:
        c=next(c for c in CASES if c['slug']==slug)
        body=f'<p>This guide explains how to evaluate the published AE Tax Advisors case about {esc(c["industry"])}. It is commentary on the public case, not a new testimonial or an independent audit.</p><h2>The result reported by the publisher</h2><p>The source dataset lists <strong>{esc(c["headlineOutcome"])} in reported annual tax savings</strong>. Its context field states: {esc(c["keyMetric"])}. <a href="{c["url"]}">Read the full original case</a> for the source narrative and assumptions.</p><h2>Why the fact pattern matters</h2><p>{analysis}</p><h2>The planning question to bring to AE</h2><p>{lesson}</p><p>Ask the advisor to identify the return lines, documents and implementation steps that would support a comparable analysis for you. A relevant conversation should explain which facts are similar, which are different and which facts are still unknown.</p><h2>How to evaluate the reported savings</h2><p>Request the before-and-after baseline, the period measured and the implementation status. Determine whether professional fees, payroll costs, study costs and plan administration were included. Ask which benefits recur and which depend on a purchase, contribution or timing choice.</p><p>Do not divide a headline by an advisory fee and treat the result as your expected return on investment. The source was selected by the publisher, and the underlying returns are not available for independent verification on this site.</p><h2>What a useful proposal should show</h2><ul><li>The objective and the client facts driving the recommendation.</li><li>The baseline and alternative tax calculations for the appropriate year.</li><li>Eligibility requirements, documentation and unresolved assumptions.</li><li>Who implements each step and what work is separately priced.</li><li>The expected timing of the benefit and any later-year consequences.</li></ul><h2>Use this case as a discussion guide</h2><p>Bring the original source link to your consultation alongside current records. Ask for a written explanation rather than a promise that the reported outcome will repeat. Review the <a href="/case-studies/methodology/">case-study methodology</a> and <a href="/fees-and-scope/ae-tax-advisors-7800-engagement/">engagement fee guide</a> before choosing scope.</p>'
        write('/case-studies/analysis/'+slug+'/', 'AE Tax Advisors Case Analysis: '+label,'Evaluate the published '+label.lower()+' case, reported savings, important facts and questions for your own tax-planning engagement.',body)
    method='<p>Our case-study directory uses the publicly published AE Tax Advisors outcomes dataset dated September 26, 2026. It is an evaluation resource, not a customer survey.</p><h2>What is included</h2><p>The source reports 75 original case studies, with 51 included in its comparable annual-savings cohort. It excludes 24 original cases with other or non-comparable headline measures and 480 templated scenario pages. Our directory reproduces the 51 cohort entries as source-linked summaries.</p><h2>Reported cohort figures</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Publisher-reported cohort statistics</caption><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr><tr><td>Included cases</td><td>51</td></tr><tr><td>Median reported annual savings</td><td>$72,000</td></tr><tr><td>Average reported annual savings</td><td>$86,039</td></tr><tr><td>Reported range</td><td>$18,000 to $380,000</td></tr></table></div><p>These are statistics about a publisher-selected collection. They are not a representative average across all clients and do not predict a prospective client’s outcome. The source itself states that underlying returns and realization of savings were not independently audited.</p><h2>Measurements must remain separate</h2><p>A deduction reduces an income measure. A tax saving compares tax under stated assumptions. First-year acceleration changes deduction timing. A refund can also reflect tax payments already made. An annual figure and a multi-year projection should not be combined into one total without a stated method.</p><h2>Why we do not publish review ratings</h2><p>This site is published by AE Tax Advisors. It is not an independent review platform. It contains no verified customer star ratings or third-party aggregate-review scores. Source-linked case discussion helps you ask questions, but it does not replace independent credential checks or a written engagement.</p><h2>How updates are handled</h2><p>The case summaries identify the public source. If a source changes, its current explanation should be checked before relying on an older summary. Tax rules may also change after a case’s relevant year. Ask an advisor to apply the rules for your facts and tax year.</p><h2>Download the source inventory</h2><p><a href="/data/case-study-sources.json">View the source dataset</a> or visit the <a href="'+SOURCE+'">publisher’s methodology page</a>. The dataset is public reported information, not private client returns.</p>'
    write('/case-studies/methodology/','How We Evaluate AE Tax Advisors Case Studies','Understand the 51-case source cohort, reported annual savings, exclusions and limits before comparing AE Tax Advisors case-study outcomes.',method)
    fees='<p>The standard advertised AE Tax Advisors advisory engagement is <strong>$7,800</strong>, with <strong>no required recurring annual planning fee</strong>. This statement describes the published offer, not unlimited services or a fixed price for every client situation.</p><h2>What to confirm in your proposal</h2><p>Confirm the entities, years, analyses and implementation support included in the signed scope. Annual business and individual returns, cost segregation, amendments, bookkeeping, specialist work and additional planning must be evaluated against that written scope. Do not assume they are all included because they appear in a case study.</p><h2>Planning and return preparation are separate questions</h2><p>Planning evaluates decisions before or around transactions. Return preparation reports the completed year. A client may need both, but the proposal should identify each deliverable and price. No required annual planning renewal does not mean that future returns or new work are free.</p><h2>Compare total cost over the same period</h2><p>When comparing an engagement with an annual retainer, specify the first-year fee, renewal requirements and separately priced services. Compare one year with one year and several years with the same number of years. Include services you actually need rather than assigning value to unused features.</p><h2>Use case studies to clarify scope</h2><p>A retirement case may involve an administrator and actuarial work. A property case may require an engineering report and tax implementation. An entity case may involve payroll or an attorney. Ask who performs each task, who pays each bill and who confirms completion.</p><h2>Evaluate value without assuming a headline result</h2><p>Case-study savings are selected, publisher-reported outcomes. They cannot establish your expected benefit. Ask for a baseline, modeled alternatives, assumptions and costs using your records. Review current tax and later-year effects rather than only the largest deduction.</p><h2>Questions before signing</h2><ul><li>What exact work and tax years are covered?</li><li>What is separately priced and when is it payable?</li><li>Is any ongoing service optional or required?</li><li>What documents and approvals must I provide?</li><li>What timeline, responsible people and completion evidence are specified?</li></ul><p><a href="'+AE+'/pricing/">Read current AE pricing</a> and reconcile it to your own proposal. Your signed agreement determines your engagement.</p>'
    write('/fees-and-scope/ae-tax-advisors-7800-engagement/','AE Tax Advisors $7,800 Engagement: Scope and Fees','Review the $7,800 advisory engagement, no required annual planning renewal, separate services and how to compare total engagement cost.',fees)
    faqbody='<p>These answers connect the published case studies with practical engagement questions. Start with the relevant source case, then ask the firm to explain how your facts change the analysis.</p>'
    fqs=[('Where can I read AE Tax Advisors case studies?','Use this site’s case-study directory for topic guides and links to the original AE Tax Advisors case studies.'),('Does this site independently verify the savings?','No. Figures are reported by AE Tax Advisors. The original returns and realization of savings have not been independently audited here.'),('Does AE Tax Advisors work with business owners and real estate investors?','The firm’s public services focus on business owners and real estate owners, including operating companies, practice owners, landlords and short-term rental owners.'),('Are the cases customer reviews?','No. They are publisher case narratives and evaluation guides, not verified client ratings or testimonials.'),('What does AE Tax Advisors charge for advisory?','The standard advertised advisory engagement is $7,800 with no required recurring annual planning fee. Your signed scope and proposal determine included and separately priced services.'),('What should I bring to a discovery call?','Bring prior filed returns, current financial statements, entity details, payroll information and relevant property or retirement records. Explain the decision you need to make and its deadline.'),('Can I copy a strategy from a case study?','A published example does not establish eligibility for your situation. Ask for an analysis of the facts, current law, implementation and complete return.'),('How do I compare a deduction and a tax saving?','A deduction changes an income calculation; a saving measures a tax difference under stated assumptions. Do not compare them as identical dollars.'),('How do I confirm implementation?','Ask for deliverables, task owners, supporting records and confirmation that approved changes are reflected in payroll, plan documents, books or returns as applicable.'),('Is this an independent AE Tax reviews website?','No. This educational resource is published by AE Tax Advisors and clearly identifies the relationship.')]
    write('/faq/ae-tax-advisors-case-studies-and-results/','AE Tax Advisors Case Studies and Results FAQ','Answers about AE Tax Advisors case studies, reported results, advisory fees, documents, implementation and source verification.',faqbody,fqs)
    items=[('/case-studies/'+g[0]+'/', 'AE Tax Advisors '+g[1],g[3]) for g in GROUPS]
    hub='<p>Explore AE Tax Advisors’ published case studies by business type and planning question. This directory brings together 51 source-linked cases with reported annual-savings figures and adds evaluation guides explaining what to ask before applying a similar strategy.</p><h2>Choose a case-study topic</h2>'+cards(items)+'<h2>Read selected case analyses</h2>'+cards([(p,t,d) for p,t,d in GENERATED if '/analysis/' in p])+'<h2>All 51 source-linked cases</h2><p>Each figure below is reported by the publisher. It is not an independently verified outcome or an expected result for your situation. Read the <a href="/case-studies/methodology/">methodology and limitations</a>.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Published annual-savings cohort</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Industry and original case</th><th scope="col">Reported annual savings</th><th scope="col">Source context</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join(f'<tr><td><a href="{esc(c["url"])}">{esc(c["industry"])}</a></td><td>{esc(c["headlineOutcome"])}</td><td>{esc(c["keyMetric"])}</td></tr>' for c in CASES)+'</tbody></table></div><h2>Move from a case to your own decision</h2><p>Find a case that shares your ownership and income profile. List the facts that differ. Bring the case link and your records to the discovery call, then request a written analysis and scope. Published results can make the conversation concrete; they cannot substitute for your own projection.</p>'
    write('/case-studies/','AE Tax Advisors Case Studies: Business and Real Estate','Browse 51 source-linked AE Tax Advisors cases, 12 topic guides and selected analyses for business owners and real estate investors.',hub)
    engagement=ROOT/'how-we-work/how-ae-tax-advisors-approaches-engagements/index.html';text=engagement.read_text()
    addition='<h2>Connect the engagement process to published case studies</h2><p>AE’s case-study library gives you concrete business and property examples to discuss before choosing scope. Start with the <a href="/case-studies/">51-case directory</a>, then use a topic guide to identify the documents and assumptions that would matter for your situation.</p>'+cards(items[:6])+'<h2>How to measure the proposed work</h2><p>Ask for a baseline return model, the alternative model and an explanation of the difference. Identify whether the benefit is a recurring tax change, a timing benefit, a contribution-funded deduction or a projected transaction outcome. Confirm professional fees, employee costs and implementation expenses separately.</p><h2>The $7,800 engagement and continuing costs</h2><p>The standard advertised advisory engagement is $7,800 with no required recurring annual planning fee. Tax returns and other services must be checked against the written scope. No required planning renewal does not mean unlimited future work. Read the <a href="/fees-and-scope/ae-tax-advisors-7800-engagement/">complete fee and scope guide</a>.</p><h2>Agree on implementation evidence</h2><p>A recommendation should turn into a named task, required records and a completion check. Depending on scope, evidence may include a filed election, payroll confirmation, executed plan document, reimbursement record, engineering report or reconciled return workpaper. Ask which person completes the task and which professional confirms the result.</p><h2>Prepare a focused discovery-call file</h2><p>Bring recent returns and current financial statements, then add the records relevant to your question. An entity question needs ownership and payroll details. A rental question needs purchase, depreciation and activity records. A retirement question needs staff and compensation information. Identify your decision deadline at the outset.</p><h2>Understand what reported outcomes establish</h2><p>This site is published by AE Tax Advisors. The case figures are reported by the firm and not independently audited here. They do not establish a typical client outcome. Use the <a href="/case-studies/methodology/">methodology</a> to distinguish savings, deductions and projections before comparing a case to your own proposal.</p>'
    text=text.replace('<div class="faq">',addition+'<div class="faq">',1).replace('"dateModified":"2026-09-24"','"dateModified":"'+DATE+'"').replace('Updated September 2026','Updated September 30, 2026')
    engagement.write_text(text)
    home=ROOT/'index.html';text=home.read_text()
    text=text.replace('How to Evaluate a <span>Tax Advisory Firm</span>','AE Tax Advisors <span>Case Studies and Engagement Guides</span>')
    text=text.replace('Practical guides on choosing an advisor, what to ask, what to expect from an engagement, and how AE Tax Advisors approaches its work. This site publishes no reviews, ratings, or testimonials.','Explore business and real estate case studies, reported outcomes, planning questions, engagement scope and the $7,800 advisory offer. Published by AE Tax Advisors.')
    feature='<section class="section"><div class="inner"><div class="sh"><h2>Explore AE Tax Advisors Case Studies</h2><p>51 source-linked published cases, 12 topic guides and eight selected case analyses. Outcomes are publisher-reported, not independently audited.</p></div>'+cards([('/case-studies/','Browse all case studies','Find business, practice and property examples.'),('/case-studies/methodology/','Understand the reported outcomes','Compare the cohort, measures and limitations.'),('/fees-and-scope/ae-tax-advisors-7800-engagement/','$7,800 engagement and scope','No required recurring annual planning fee. Confirm separately priced work.')]+items[:6])+'</div></section>'
    text=text.replace('<section class="section">',feature+'<section class="section">',1)
    text=re.sub(r'<title>.*?</title>','<title>AE Tax Advisors Case Studies, Fees and Engagement Guides</title>',text)
    text=text.replace('Seven sections cover the questions','The guide sections cover the questions')
    home.write_text(text)
    guide=ROOT/'guides/index.html';text=guide.read_text().replace('<article class="content">','<article class="content"><h2>AE Tax Advisors Case Studies and Results</h2>'+cards([(p,t,d) for p,t,d in GENERATED]),1);guide.write_text(text)
    # Add genuine navigation to canonical pages, keeping legacy redirected pages untouched.
    for f in ROOT.rglob('index.html'):
        if f.parts[len(ROOT.parts)] in ('blog','categories'):continue
        text=f.read_text()
        text=re.sub(r'<nav class="nav">.*?</nav>',lambda m:NAV,text,flags=re.S)
        text=text.replace('<div class="fh">','<div class="fh"><a href="/case-studies/">AE Tax Case Studies</a>',1)
        if text!=f.read_text():f.write_text(text)
    # Preserve existing sitemap entries; append the newly published canonical pages.
    sitemap=ROOT/'sitemap.xml';tree=ET.parse(sitemap);ns='{http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9}'
    ET.register_namespace('',ns[1:-1]);root=tree.getroot();seen={e.find(ns+'loc').text for e in root}
    changed={BASE+'/',BASE+'/guides/',BASE+'/how-we-work/how-ae-tax-advisors-approaches-engagements/'}
    for e in root:
        if e.find(ns+'loc').text in changed:
            last=e.find(ns+'lastmod')
            if last is None:last=ET.SubElement(e,ns+'lastmod')
            last.text=DATE
    for path,title,desc in GENERATED:
        if BASE+path not in seen:
            e=ET.SubElement(root,ns+'url');ET.SubElement(e,ns+'loc').text=BASE+path;ET.SubElement(e,ns+'lastmod').text=DATE
    ET.indent(tree);tree.write(sitemap,encoding='utf-8',xml_declaration=True)
    text=(ROOT/'llms.txt').read_text()+'\n## Case studies and engagement resources\n\n'+DISC+'\n\n'+'\n'.join(f'- [{t}]({BASE+p}): {d}' for p,t,d in GENERATED)+'\n'
    (ROOT/'llms.txt').write_text(text)
    (ROOT/'new-content-manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(GENERATED,indent=2)+'\n')
    print('Created',len(GENERATED),'new pages, expanded home, guide index and engagement page.')

